      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHAT A WROUGHT (7) has a fair record and proved too classy last time to win by 4 lengths at Shepparton in a handy 25.72 beating Billy Boy Reuben. Yet to win out of this box but has been in the placings five times from six starts. Makes plenty of appeal if runs up to latest. ASTON MONSOON (1) is a capable type and proved too classy last time to win by 0.7 lengths at this track in a handy 23.20 beating Paw Jelani. The form out of the last run is proven to be strong. Shapes as a top winning chance on latest effort. NO MORE EXTRAS (8) had won two in a row before finishing third (31.08) last time at The Meadows. Has a good record here including three wins. Expected to feature. TRAJECTORY (2) will give backers a sight.",
